PROMPT Given $X∼\text{Po}(2),$ compute $P(X=5),$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.
END SOLUTION If $X∼\text{Po}(\lambda ),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:

$$
f(x)=\frac{{\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\lambda }}{x!}
$$

Here, $X∼\text{Po}(2),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is

$$
f(x)=\frac{{2}^{x}{e}^{-2}}{x!}.
$$

Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =f(5) \\  & =\frac{{2}^{5}{e}^{-2}}{5!} \\  & ≈0.0361.\end{aligned}
$$
